### Include macOS Frameworks in Bundle

Source: https://tauri.app/distribute/macos-application-bundle

List system or custom frameworks and dylib files to be included in the macOS application bundle. System frameworks can be referenced by name.

```json
{
  "bundle": {
    "macOS": {
      "frameworks": [
        "CoreAudio",
        "./libs/libmsodbcsql.18.dylib",
        "./frameworks/MyApp.framework"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Bundle Configuration Example

Source: https://tauri.app/reference/config

Contains settings for the application bundler, including platform-specific configurations for Android, iOS, Linux, macOS, and Windows.

```json
{
  "active": false,
  "android": {
    "autoIncrementVersionCode": false,
    "minSdkVersion": 24
  },
  "createUpdaterArtifacts": false,
  "iOS": {
    "minimumSystemVersion": "14.0"
  },
  "icon": [],
  "linux": {
    "appimage": {
      "bundleMediaFramework": false,
      "files": {}
    },
    "deb": {
      "files": {}
    },
    "rpm": {
      "epoch": 0,
      "files": {},
      "release": "1"
    }
  },
  "macOS": {
    "dmg": {
      "appPosition": {
        "x": 180,
        "y": 170
      },
      "applicationFolderPosition": {
        "x": 480,
        "y": 170
      },
      "windowSize": {
        "height": 400,
        "width": 660
      }
    },
    "files": {},
    "hardenedRuntime": true,
    "minimumSystemVersion": "10.13"
  },
  "targets": "all",
  "useLocalToolsDir": false,
  "windows": {
    "allowDowngrades": true,
    "certificateThumbprint": null,
    "digestAlgorithm": null,
    "minimumWebview2Version": null,
    "nsis": null,
    "signCommand": null,
    "timestampUrl": null,
    "tsp": false,
    "webviewInstallMode": {
      "silent": true,
      "type": "downloadBootstrapper"
    },
    "wix": null
  }
}
```

### Configuration > MacConfig > frameworks

Source: https://tauri.app/reference/config

The `frameworks` option is a list of macOS X frameworks to bundle with the application. Framework names can be provided without the `.framework` extension, and Tauri will search standard locations. Paths to specific frameworks are also supported.

--------------------------------

### Including macOS frameworks

Source: https://tauri.app/distribute/macos-application-bundle

You can include additional macOS frameworks or dylib files in your application bundle by listing them in the `bundle.macOS.frameworks` configuration. This list can contain system frameworks (referenced by name) or custom frameworks and dylibs (referenced by their path relative to the `src-tauri` directory).

--------------------------------

### Configuration > MacConfig

Source: https://tauri.app/reference/config

The `MacConfig` section provides settings for macOS bundles, including bundle name, version, DMG settings, entitlements, exception domain, files, frameworks, hardened runtime, Info.plist, minimum system version, provider short name, and signing identity.

